  "body": "## What changed\n\nThis change pins the 2D Pocket with Outside containment under the ring-link law of #3747.\nThe test pin asserts that link moves between rings stay in the plane as feed moves round a disc, and each lift has a named reason.\nThe decision record `docs/decisions/3747-in-plane-ring-links.md` is updated to note that a 2D Pocket with Outside containment (`around_part: true`) takes the ring-link law.\n\n## Readings\n\n- `outside_pocket_rings_round_a_disc_do_not_lift`: 0 lifts, 0 re-entries, in-plane floor feed moves confirmed.\n- `outside_pocket_dog_bone_names_each_lift`: each lift is named, no overcut, no crossing feeds.\n- `failed_ring_link_lifts_to_the_users_pass_plane`: fixture clamp lifts are named and verified against the user's pass link plane.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `camcraft-motion`: `crates/motion/tests/pass_start_levels/pocket_outside.rs::outside_pocket_rings_round_a_disc_do_not_lift`\n- `camcraft-motion`: `crates/motion/tests/pass_start_levels/pocket_outside.rs::outside_pocket_dog_bone_names_each_lift`\n- `camcraft-motion`: `crates/motion/tests/pass_start_levels/pocket_outside.rs::failed_ring_link_lifts_to_the_users_pass_plane`\n\n## What was not exercised\n\n- 3D operations.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #3820\n",
